25,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"We are losing an hour a day to copying records, and misrouted deliveries are happening because of inconsistent addresses.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,May,,"Our developers are tied up until Q3, and the coordination group is severely understaffed.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Customer plant network coverage is terrible, and projects requiring daily entry from everyone usually fail.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital budget is frozen, but we have a software allowance. Also, per-head licenses are getting more expensive.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Most standardization efforts fail without owners, but vendor queries are being repeated because of poor record sharing.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, if the coordination group is that thin, any project adding to their manual work will fail.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly, Daisuke. We can't afford a tool that requires more manual oversight from a skeleton crew.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the capital budget is frozen, we should avoid any hardware or heavy infrastructure.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree, Shunichi. We must stick to the software allowance and avoid scaling license costs.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, the address issues you found match the vendor query problems I saw. It's a data duplication problem.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,It seems we have a lot of wasted time on basic data entry and correction.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, does the failure of ""daily entry"" tools mean we should avoid apps that require constant updates?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Yes, May. If it feels like a chore for the staff, they just stop using it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We need something that fits the software budget and doesn't require a massive rollout of new licenses.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"And it should be a tool that provides a lasting resource, not just a temporary standardization attempt.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
