50,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The candidates are A: Field Service App, B: Training Studio, C: Supplier Data Hub, and D: Workflow Assistant. I prefer C.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,May,,"C sounds like it might add to the coordination burden, but D requires developers we don't have.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"A is a disaster waiting to happen given the network coverage and the ""daily entry"" failure pattern.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"B might be a fixed-fee production, but C's license costs could climb if it's per-head.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Kenji,,C addresses the misrouted deliveries and vendor query issues Daisuke and I found.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, C is a repository, not a daily task. It should reduce the coordination group's manual work.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,May,,That's a fair point. D is definitely out since the developers are busy until Q3.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"B is too niche. C solves a systemic problem across units, provided it doesn't require daily manual updates.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If C is a central catalog, we can manage the software allowance. It's more stable than A.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I agree. C is the only one that fixes the actual errors happening on the floor.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm voting for C. It stops the waste of time we're seeing.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,May,,I can support C if it actually reduces the manual workload for the staff.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I vote C. It avoids the network risks of A and the failure pattern of D.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,C is the most fiscally responsible choice given the budget freeze. I vote C.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Kenji,,C it is! It's the most logical way to stop repeating the same mistakes.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
